; Load-time rejections of the rich `:heads` spelling. Three separate
; kinds so each condition is reported once against its own kind name.
;
;   `mixed`      — `:names` and `(head …)` in one `(head-set …)`. The two
;                  spellings are exclusive, exactly as `(member-set …)`'s
;                  `:values` and `(member …)` are.
;   `duplicated` — the same `:name` twice. A head-set is a *set*; two
;                  entries for one head means two answers to "how many".
;   `backwards`  — `:min` above `:max`. An empty range admits nothing, so
;                  no document could ever satisfy the slot.
(plugin :name gfx :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name vertex)
  (form :name fragment)

  (value-kind :name mixed
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set
      :names [vertex]
      (head :name fragment)))

  (value-kind :name duplicated
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set
      (head :name vertex :max 1)
      (head :name vertex :max 2)))

  (value-kind :name backwards
    :underlying form
    :heads (head-set
      (head :name vertex :min 3 :max 1))))

; A no-op literal, not a `(vertex)`: a plugin whose manifest failed to
; load is dropped entirely, so any data form would cascade into an
; `unknown_form` that has nothing to do with what this case is about.
; Same reason `member-rich-and-values-conflict` ends in a bare `42`.
42
